20Summarise%20what%20stands%20out." target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 text-sm disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-60 hover:bg-black dark:hover:bg-black-500 hover:text-white px-3 py-2 w-full justify-start" data-menu-item="true"><!--[0--><!----><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="shrink-0  svg-icon IconServiceOpenAI" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16.8 8.18a4.07 4.07 0 0 0-4.98-4.99 4.07 4.07 0 0 0-6.8 1.83 4.07 4.07 0 0 0-1.83 6.8 4.07 4.07 0 0 0 4.99 4.99 4.07 4.07 0 0 0 6.8-1.83 4.07 4.07 0 0 0 1.83-6.8M15.1 4.9c.72.72 1.02 1.7.9 2.64L12.6 5.6a.5.5 0 0 0-.46 0L8.18 7.88v-1.5q0-.16.14-.26l3.02-1.74c1.2-.67 2.74-.5 3.76.52m-5.1 3 1.82 1.05v2.1L10 12.11l-1.82-1.06v-2.1zM5.8 6.01a3.15 3.15 0 0 1 5.07-2.44L7.48 5.54a.5.5 0 0 0-.23.4v4.58l-1.3-.75a.3.3 0 0 1-.15-.26zM3.03 8.13c.27-.98.97-1.73 1.85-2.1v3.92c0 .16.09.32.23.4l3.97 2.29-1.3.75a.3.3 0 0 1-.3 0l-3.02-1.74a3.15 3.15 0 0 1-1.43-3.52M4.9 15.1a3.1 3.1 0 0 1-.9-2.64l3.4 1.95q.22.12.46 0l3.96-2.29v1.5q0 .16-.14.26l-3.02 1.74c-1.2.67-2.74.5-3.76-.52m9.3-1.12a3.15 3.15 0 0 1-5.07 2.44l3.39-1.96a.5.5 0 0 0 .23-.4V9.48l1.3.75q.15.09.15.26zm2.77-2.11a3.1 3.1 0 0 1-1.85 2.1v-3.92a.5.5 0 0 0-.23-.4l-3.97-2.29 1.3-.75a.3.3 0 0 1 .3 0l3.02 1.74c1.18.7 1.8 2.13 1.43 3.52"/></svg><!----><!--]--> <!--[2-->Open ChatGPT<!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!----></a><!----> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!--]--></div></div><!----></div> <!--[--><article class="px-6  mt-15 lg:mt-20 "><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[0--><div class="mx-auto max-w-prose"><!--[0--><h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-headline font-normal">AI moves from on-the-side to built-in</h2><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class="md text-lg mt-7"><!---->Coding assistants and agents have pulled ahead as the dominant use case for AI (66%), outpacing even general-purpose LLM-powered chatbots (63%). It’s a sign that AI has become less sidekick and more infrastructure, built right into the tools technologists already use. The overwhelming majority of respondents now use coding assistants and agents daily (73%), with nearly a third of daily users spending upwards of four hours.<!----></div><!--]--></div><!--]--></div></article><article class="px-6 relative border-t border-b border-transparent bg-black-100 py-10 lg:py-20 dark:border-black-500 dark:bg-black mt-15 lg:mt-[8vh] "><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[-1--><div class="group justify-center gap-15 md:grid md:grid-cols-10 pb-6 lg:pb-0"><div class="col-span-5 "><!--[-1--><p class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-black-400 dark:text-black-300"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block h-3 w-3 shrink-0" style="background: var(--chapter-primary, var(--color-orange))"></span> <!--[0--><a class="hover:underline" href="/2026/ai/data#ai-usage">AI usage</a><!--]--></p> <h3 class="font-headline text-3xl font-normal md:text-4xl">31% of daily AI users use it for 4+ hours/day</h3> <!--[0--><div class="md mt-4 text-base text-black-400 dark:text-black-300"><!---->Of the over 70% of respondents who use AI daily, 31% use it over four hours per day.<!----></div><!--]--> <!--[0--><a href="/2026/ai/data/ai-daily" class="absolute right-3 bottom-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-2 text-sm hover:bg-black hover:text-white dark:hover:bg-black-500" aria-label="Permalink: 31% of daily AI users use it for 4+ hours/day">View and share <!----><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="svg-icon IconLink" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8.93 6.81a5 5 0 0 1 3.56 1.95l-1.2.9a3.4 3.4 0 0 0-5.11-.37L3.7 11.77l-.11.12a3.4 3.4 0 0 0 4.9 4.67l1.41-1.4 1.06 1.05-1.42 1.43a4.9 4.9 0 0 1-6.92-6.92h.01l2.49-2.49a5 5 0 0 1 3.8-1.42m5.44-5.75a4.9 4.9 0 0 1 3.48 8.29l-2.5 2.5a4.9 4.9 0 0 1-7.37-.54l1.2-.9a3.4 3.4 0 0 0 5.11.37l2.48-2.47a3.4 3.4 0 0 0-4.8-4.8l-1.41 1.4-.53-.52-.53-.53 1.42-1.42h.01a5 5 0 0 1 3.44-1.38"/></svg><!----><!----></a><!--]--><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--></div> <figure class="chart-reveal col-span-5 mt-10 lg:mt-0 [&amp;>svg]:h-auto [&amp;>svg]:w-full"><!--[--><!--$s2--><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="590" height="319" viewBox="0 0 590 319" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMin meet" role="img" aria-label="31% of daily AI users use it for 4+ hours/day" aria-describedby="s2-desc" font-family="Stack Sans Text, system-ui, sans-serif"><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[0--><desc id="s2-desc">4+ hours/day 31%, 2-4 hours/day 24%, 1-2 hours/day 25%, &lt;1 hour every day 12%, &lt;1 hour and not every day 7%, None 1% · All Respondents · n = 10,926</desc><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--[--><g role="presentation"><rect x="0" y="0" width="590" height="44" fill="transparent"></rect><rect x="0" y="0" width="477.88" height="44" fill="var(--chart-focus, #5074ef)"></rect><!--[0--><text x="493.88" y="20" font-size="25" font-family="Stack Sans Headline, system-ui, sans-serif" font-weight="600" fill="var(--chart-ink, #201c1d)">31%</text><text x="493.88" y="42" font-size="15" fill="var(--chart-muted, #636261)">4+ hours/day</text><!--]--></g><g role="presentation"><rect x="0" y="52" width="590" height="44" fill="transparent"></rect><rect x="0" y="52" width="369.97" height="44" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><!--[-1--><!--]--></g><g role="presentation"><rect x="0" y="104" width="590" height="44" fill="transparent"></rect><rect x="0" y="104" width="385.39" height="44" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><!--[-1--><!--]--></g><g role="presentation"><rect x="0" y="156" width="590" height="44" fill="transparent"></rect><rect x="0" y="156" width="184.99" height="44" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><!--[-1--><!--]--></g><g role="presentation"><rect x="0" y="208" width="590" height="44" fill="transparent"></rect><rect x="0" y="208" width="107.91" height="44" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><!--[-1--><!--]--></g><g role="presentation"><rect x="0" y="260" width="590" height="44" fill="transparent"></rect><rect x="0" y="260" width="15.42" height="44" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><!--[-1--><!--]--></g><!--]--><!----><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--></svg><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!----> <figcaption class="sr-only"><!--[0--><div class="overflow-auto"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead><tr class="border-b border-black-150 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold "></th><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold text-right">Respondents</th><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold text-right">Percent</th><!--]--></tr></thead><tbody><!--[--><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">4+ hours/day</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">3,378</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">30.9%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">2-4 hours/day</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">2,636</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">24.1%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">1-2 hours/day</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">2,765</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">25.3%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">&lt;1 hour every day</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">1,335</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">12.2%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">&lt;1 hour and not every day</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">763</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">7.0%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">None</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">49</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">0.5%</td><!--]--></tr><!--]--></tbody></table></div><!--]--><!----></figcaption></figure></div><!--]--></div></article><article class="px-6  mt-15 lg:mt-20 "><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[0--><div class="mx-auto max-w-prose"><!--[0--><h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-headline font-normal">Despite plenty of societal concern about AI, survey respondents retain a fairly positive view of the technology.</h2><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class="md text-lg mt-7"><!---->When asked about overall attitude toward AI tools, favorable views outnumber unfavorable ones by almost 3 to 1. But “favorable” doesn&#39;t mean “unconditionally positive.” Developers aren&#39;t simply handing AI the keys to important decisions. When asked when it’s acceptable to trust AI, 48% indicate they trust AI when they can easily validate the answers and only 16% extend that trust to most tasks that are not important work decisions. The sweet spot where most AI users land is trusting AI when they understand what it’s working on, such as with familiar code (67% currently use AI with this) or when debugging or refactoring (61% currently use AI with this). That’s why human-in-the-loop is the dominant mode of working with these tools.<!----></div><!--]--></div><!--]--></div></article><article class="px-6  mt-15 lg:mt-20 "><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[1--><blockquote class="mx-auto max-w-6xl text-center"><p class="font-headline text-[clamp(var(--text-3xl),3vw+0.5rem,var(--text-5xl))] leading-[1.1em] font-normal text-balance">“This is where I personally feel the importance of human judgment. If you leave it up to chance, if you leave it up to the roll of the dice of the LLM, you're not gonna get the specificity. Everything I've been doing and everything my team's been doing is imagining AI as an exoskeleton, like a Tony Stark augmentation, as opposed to an empty Ultron with nobody inside. Which nobody wants.”</p> <!--[0--><footer class="mt-8 text-lg text-black-400 md:mt-12 dark:text-black-300"><div class="md"><!----><a href="https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/01/13/vibe-code-anything-in-a-hanselminute/">Scott Hanselman, VP of Developer Community at Microsoft</a><!----></div></footer><!--]--></blockquote><!--]--></div></article><article class="px-6  mt-15 lg:mt-20 "><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[0--><div class="mx-auto max-w-prose"><!--[0--><h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-headline font-normal">The right tool for the job</h2><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class="md text-lg mt-7"><!---->The same caution shows up in how people choose (and choose against) certain tools. Developers switching to new AI tools are doing it mostly because the output is better (25%) or because their organization required it (11%).<!----></div><!--]--></div><!--]--></div></article><article class="px-6 relative border-t border-b border-transparent bg-black-100 py-10 lg:py-20 dark:border-black-500 dark:bg-black mt-15 lg:mt-[8vh] "><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[-1--><div class="group justify-center gap-15 md:grid md:grid-cols-10 pb-6 lg:pb-0"><div class="col-span-5 "><!--[-1--><p class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-black-400 dark:text-black-300"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block h-3 w-3 shrink-0" style="background: var(--chapter-primary, var(--color-orange))"></span> <!--[0--><a class="hover:underline" href="/2026/ai/data#ai-at-work">AI at work</a><!--]--></p> <h3 class="font-headline text-3xl font-normal md:text-4xl">25% switch AI tools due to better output quality</h3> <!--[0--><div class="md mt-4 text-base text-black-400 dark:text-black-300"><!---->Seeking superior output quality is the single largest reason developers switch AI tools, though a third (34%) retained their original tool choices over the past year. For all the concerns over token costs, only 6% switched because of costs.<!----></div><!--]--> <!--[0--><a href="/2026/ai/data/ai-tool-switch" class="absolute right-3 bottom-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-2 text-sm hover:bg-black hover:text-white dark:hover:bg-black-500" aria-label="Permalink: 25% switch AI tools due to better output quality">View and share <!----><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="svg-icon IconLink" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8.93 6.81a5 5 0 0 1 3.56 1.95l-1.2.9a3.4 3.4 0 0 0-5.11-.37L3.7 11.77l-.11.12a3.4 3.4 0 0 0 4.9 4.67l1.41-1.4 1.06 1.05-1.42 1.43a4.9 4.9 0 0 1-6.92-6.92h.01l2.49-2.49a5 5 0 0 1 3.8-1.42m5.44-5.75a4.9 4.9 0 0 1 3.48 8.29l-2.5 2.5a4.9 4.9 0 0 1-7.37-.54l1.2-.9a3.4 3.4 0 0 0 5.11.37l2.48-2.47a3.4 3.4 0 0 0-4.8-4.8l-1.41 1.4-.53-.52-.53-.53 1.42-1.42h.01a5 5 0 0 1 3.44-1.38"/></svg><!----><!----></a><!--]--><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--></div> <figure class="chart-reveal col-span-5 mt-10 lg:mt-0 [&amp;>svg]:h-auto [&amp;>svg]:w-full"><!--[--><!--$s3--><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="590" height="496.1" viewBox="0 0 590 496.1" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMin meet" role="img" aria-label="25% switch AI tools due to better output quality" aria-describedby="s3-desc" font-family="Stack Sans Text, system-ui, sans-serif"><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[0--><desc id="s3-desc">No 34%, Better output quality 25%, My organization required it 11%, Better integration 7%, Yes — lower cost 6%, Better agent support 4%, Another reason 4%, The old tool became limited 3%, and 4 more · All Respondents · n = 13,144</desc><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--[--><rect x="0" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="0" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="49.83" y="109.32" width="41.83" height="303.68" fill="var(--chart-focus, #5074ef)"></rect><rect x="49.83" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="99.66" y="279.38" width="41.83" height="133.62" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="99.66" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="149.49" y="327.97" width="41.83" height="85.03" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="149.49" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="199.32" y="340.12" width="41.83" height="72.88" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="199.32" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="249.15" y="364.41" width="41.83" height="48.59" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="249.15" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="298.98" y="364.41" width="41.83" height="48.59" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="298.98" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="348.81" y="376.56" width="41.83" height="36.44" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="348.81" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="398.64" y="388.71" width="41.83" height="24.29" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="398.64" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="448.47" y="388.71" width="41.83" height="24.29" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="448.47" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="498.3" y="400.85" width="41.83" height="12.15" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="498.3" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="548.13" y="400.85" width="41.83" height="12.15" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="548.13" y="0" width="41.83" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><!--]--><!--[0--><text x="49.83" y="454" font-size="25" font-family="Stack Sans Headline, system-ui, sans-serif" font-weight="600" fill="var(--chart-ink, #201c1d)">25%</text><text x="49.83" y="476" font-size="15" fill="var(--chart-muted, #636261)">Better output quality</text><!--]--><!----><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--></svg><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!----> <figcaption class="sr-only"><!--[0--><div class="overflow-auto"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead><tr class="border-b border-black-150 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold "></th><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold text-right">Respondents</th><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold text-right">Percent</th><!--]--></tr></thead><tbody><!--[--><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">No</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">4,423</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">33.7%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">Yes — better output quality</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">3,305</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">25.1%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">Yes — my organization required or recommended a different tool</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">1,394</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">10.6%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">Yes — better integration with my workflow or development environment</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">975</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">7.4%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">Yes — lower cost</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">835</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">6.4%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">Yes — better support for agents, automation, or coding workflows</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">487</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">3.7%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">Yes — another reason (write in)</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">466</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">3.6%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">Yes — the previous tool became too expensive, limited, or unavailable</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">433</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">3.3%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">Yes — better security, privacy, or compliance</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">283</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">2.2%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">Yes — access to a preferred model or provider</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">280</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">2.1%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">Yes — for a specific feature</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">179</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">1.4%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">Not applicable — I do not use AI tools for work</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">84</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">0.6%</td><!--]--></tr><!--]--></tbody></table></div><!--]--><!----></figcaption></figure></div><!--]--></div></article><article class="px-6  mt-15 lg:mt-20 "><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[0--><div class="mx-auto max-w-prose"><!--[-1--><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class="md text-lg "><!----><p>What are they using? Claude Code (66%) and GitHub Copilot (59%) are the leaders for coding agents. Respondents are using LangChain (30%) and OpenAI Agents SDK (24%) for orchestration and Make (39%) and n8n (33%) for automation. AI memory and agent orchestration tools show a notable gap between current adoption and stated interest, suggesting that the category is still finding its footing. Coding agents, meanwhile, are a more mature market with clear leaders emerging. </p>
<p>That selectivity becomes very clear once you look at where AI is actually being put to work. Basically, developers trust AI with machines but not with people. AI use is common, and commonly accepted, across code generation, debugging, testing, and understanding unfamiliar codebases. Even secondary review functions—analyzing telemetry, reviewing pull requests, hunting for security issues—are seeing meaningful AI adoption.</p><!----></div><!--]--></div><!--]--></div></article><article class="px-6  mt-15 lg:mt-20 "><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[0--><div class="mx-auto max-w-prose"><!--[0--><h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-headline font-normal">The human difference</h2><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class="md text-lg mt-7"><!---->But the moment the task shifts toward human communication or creative output—writing emails, generating multimedia, anything requiring a feel for what people want—usage falls off a cliff. The same split shows up in perceived usefulness: technical tasks like implementation and debugging are both useful or very useful to 70%+ of survey respondents, while communication and design lag behind, landing in “slop” territory with 35% and 49% respectively finding AI useful or very useful in those areas.<!----></div><!--]--></div><!--]--></div></article><article class="px-6 relative border-t border-b border-transparent bg-black-100 py-10 lg:py-20 dark:border-black-500 dark:bg-black mt-15 lg:mt-[8vh] "><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[-1--><div class="group justify-center gap-15 md:grid md:grid-cols-10 pb-6 lg:pb-0"><div class="col-span-5 md:order-last"><!--[-1--><p class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-black-400 dark:text-black-300"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block h-3 w-3 shrink-0" style="background: var(--chapter-primary, var(--color-orange))"></span> <!--[-1--><!--]--></p> <h3 class="font-headline text-3xl font-normal md:text-4xl"></h3> <!--[0--><div class="md mt-4 text-base text-black-400 dark:text-black-300"><!---->The top 5 tasks that respondents are currently using AI or AI agents for<!----></div><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--></div> <figure class="chart-reveal col-span-5 mt-10 lg:mt-0 [&amp;>svg]:h-auto [&amp;>svg]:w-full"><!--[--><!--$s4--><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="590" height="605" viewBox="0 0 590 605" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMin meet" role="img" aria-label="&lt;p>Which parts of your workflow are you currently integrating into AI or using AI agents to accomplish? Will they be more or less integrated over the next year? Please select one for each scenario.&lt;/p>" aria-describedby="s4-desc" font-family="Stack Sans Text, system-ui, sans-serif"><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[0--><desc id="s4-desc">Generating code in a familiar area 69%, Debugging, troubleshooting, or refactoring code 64%, Answering straightforward technical questions 59%, Writing or improving tests 58%, Generating code in an unfamiliar area 56% · All Respondents · n = 12,547</desc><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--[--><g role="presentation"><rect x="0" y="0" width="252" height="302" fill="var(--chart-focus, #5074ef)" fill-opacity="1"></rect><!--[0--><text x="10" y="287" font-size="15" fill="var(--chart-on-focus, #ffffff)">Generating code in a famili…</text><text x="10" y="265" font-size="25" font-family="Stack Sans Headline, system-ui, sans-serif" font-weight="600" fill="var(--chart-on-focus, #ffffff)">69%</text><!--]--></g><g role="presentation"><rect x="0" y="310" width="252" height="280" fill="var(--chart-focus, #5074ef)" fill-opacity="0.825"></rect><!--[0--><text x="10" y="575" font-size="15" fill="var(--chart-on-focus, #ffffff)">Debugging, troubleshooting,…</text><text x="10" y="553" font-size="25" font-family="Stack Sans Headline, system-ui, sans-serif" font-weight="600" fill="var(--chart-on-focus, #ffffff)">64%</text><!--]--></g><g role="presentation"><rect x="260" y="0" width="330" height="196" fill="var(--chart-focus, #5074ef)" fill-opacity="0.65"></rect><!--[0--><text x="270" y="181" font-size="15" fill="var(--chart-on-focus, #ffffff)">Answering straightforward technical q…</text><text x="270" y="159" font-size="25" font-family="Stack Sans Headline, system-ui, sans-serif" font-weight="600" fill="var(--chart-on-focus, #ffffff)">59%</text><!--]--></g><g role="presentation"><rect x="260" y="204" width="330" height="192" fill="var(--chart-focus, #5074ef)" fill-opacity="0.4750000000000001"></rect><!--[0--><text x="270" y="381" font-size="15" fill="var(--chart-ink, #201c1d)">Writing or improving tests</text><text x="270" y="359" font-size="25" font-family="Stack Sans Headline, system-ui, sans-serif" font-weight="600" fill="var(--chart-ink, #201c1d)">58%</text><!--]--></g><g role="presentation"><rect x="260" y="404" width="330" height="186" fill="var(--chart-focus, #5074ef)" fill-opacity="0.30000000000000004"></rect><!--[0--><text x="270" y="575" font-size="15" fill="var(--chart-ink, #201c1d)">Generating code in an unfamiliar area</text><text x="270" y="553" font-size="25" font-family="Stack Sans Headline, system-ui, sans-serif" font-weight="600" fill="var(--chart-ink, #201c1d)">56%</text><!--]--></g><!--]--><!----><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--></svg><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!----> <figcaption class="sr-only"><!--[0--><div class="overflow-auto"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead><tr class="border-b border-black-150 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold "></th><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold text-right">Respondents</th><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold text-right">Percent</th><!--]--></tr></thead><tbody><!--[--><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">Generating code in a familiar area</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">8,402</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">69.3%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">Debugging, troubleshooting, or refactoring code</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">7,684</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">63.8%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">Answering straightforward technical questions</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">7,017</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">59.4%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">Writing or improving tests</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">6,915</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">58.1%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">Generating code in an unfamiliar area</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">6,707</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">56.0%</td><!--]--></tr><!--]--></tbody></table></div><!--]--><!----></figcaption></figure></div><!--]--></div></article><article class="px-6  mt-15 lg:mt-20 "><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[0--><div class="mx-auto max-w-prose"><!--[-1--><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class="md text-lg "><!---->The inevitable takeaway is that technologists see AI as very good at technical problems with checkable answers, and considerably less good at solving the other everyday problems of work. A significant chunk of respondents who avoid AI completely do so out of concern for their own skills, privacy, or the technology’s enormous ethical and environmental footprint.<!----></div><!--]--></div><!--]--></div></article><article class="px-6 relative border-t border-b border-transparent bg-black-100 py-10 lg:py-20 dark:border-black-500 dark:bg-black mt-15 lg:mt-[8vh] mb-10 lg:mb-[8vh]"><div class="mx-auto max-w-310"><!--[-1--><div class="group justify-center gap-15 md:grid md:grid-cols-10 pb-6 lg:pb-0"><div class="col-span-5 md:order-last"><!--[-1--><p class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-black-400 dark:text-black-300"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block h-3 w-3 shrink-0" style="background: var(--chapter-primary, var(--color-orange))"></span> <!--[0--><a class="hover:underline" href="/2026/ai/data#ai-at-work">AI at work</a><!--]--></p> <h3 class="font-headline text-3xl font-normal md:text-4xl"></h3> <!--[0--><div class="md mt-4 text-base text-black-400 dark:text-black-300"><!---->6 out of 10 users cite a reason to avoid using AI at work or school, losing job skills is a top concern.<!----></div><!--]--> <!--[0--><a href="/2026/ai/data/ai-avoid" class="absolute right-3 bottom-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-2 text-sm hover:bg-black hover:text-white dark:hover:bg-black-500" aria-label="Permalink: ">View and share <!----><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="svg-icon IconLink" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8.93 6.81a5 5 0 0 1 3.56 1.95l-1.2.9a3.4 3.4 0 0 0-5.11-.37L3.7 11.77l-.11.12a3.4 3.4 0 0 0 4.9 4.67l1.41-1.4 1.06 1.05-1.42 1.43a4.9 4.9 0 0 1-6.92-6.92h.01l2.49-2.49a5 5 0 0 1 3.8-1.42m5.44-5.75a4.9 4.9 0 0 1 3.48 8.29l-2.5 2.5a4.9 4.9 0 0 1-7.37-.54l1.2-.9a3.4 3.4 0 0 0 5.11.37l2.48-2.47a3.4 3.4 0 0 0-4.8-4.8l-1.41 1.4-.53-.52-.53-.53 1.42-1.42h.01a5 5 0 0 1 3.44-1.38"/></svg><!----><!----></a><!--]--><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--></div> <figure class="chart-reveal col-span-5 mt-10 lg:mt-0 [&amp;>svg]:h-auto [&amp;>svg]:w-full"><!--[--><!--$s5--><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="590" height="496.1" viewBox="0 0 590 496.1" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMin meet" role="img" aria-label="&lt;p>Do you try to avoid using AI tools or agents at work or school? Select the option below that most accurately reflects your reasoning.&lt;/p>" aria-describedby="s5-desc" font-family="Stack Sans Text, system-ui, sans-serif"><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[0--><desc id="s5-desc">I don't avoid AI 41%, Losing skills to AI 17%, Morals/ethics 15%, Privacy or security 13%, Environmental concerns 8%, Other 3%, Lack of training 3% · All Respondents · n = 13,857</desc><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--[--><rect x="0" y="0" width="77.43" height="413" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="0" y="0" width="77.43" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="85.43" y="241.76" width="77.43" height="171.24" fill="var(--chart-focus, #5074ef)"></rect><rect x="85.43" y="0" width="77.43" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="170.86" y="261.9" width="77.43" height="151.1" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="170.86" y="0" width="77.43" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="256.29" y="282.05" width="77.43" height="130.95" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="256.29" y="0" width="77.43" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="341.72" y="332.41" width="77.43" height="80.59" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="341.72" y="0" width="77.43" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="427.15" y="382.78" width="77.43" height="30.22" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="427.15" y="0" width="77.43" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><rect x="512.58" y="382.78" width="77.43" height="30.22" fill="var(--chart-rest, #998b7a)"></rect><rect x="512.58" y="0" width="77.43" height="413" fill="transparent" role="presentation"></rect><!--]--><!--[0--><text x="85.43" y="454" font-size="25" font-family="Stack Sans Headline, system-ui, sans-serif" font-weight="600" fill="var(--chart-ink, #201c1d)">17%</text><text x="85.43" y="476" font-size="15" fill="var(--chart-muted, #636261)">Losing skills to AI</text><!--]--><!----><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--><!--[-1--><!--]--></svg><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!----> <figcaption class="sr-only"><!--[0--><div class="overflow-auto"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead><tr class="border-b border-black-150 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold "></th><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold text-right">Respondents</th><th scope="col" class="px-2 pb-2 font-semibold text-right">Percent</th><!--]--></tr></thead><tbody><!--[--><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">I do not avoid using AI at work or school</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">5,728</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">41.3%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  ">Concern over losing job skills or training an AI to replace you</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">2,367</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top  text-right tabular-nums">17.1%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 ">Moral or ethical concerns</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">2,108</td><td class="px-2 py-1.5 align-top bg-black-100 dark:bg-black-500 text-right tabular-nums">15.2%</td><!--]--></tr><tr class="border-b border-black-150 last:border-0 dark:border-black-500"><!--[--><td class="p